WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.332
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:09.500
SPEAKER: The COVID-19 pandemic
has affected people's health,

00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:11.530
finances, and daily lives.

00:00:11.530 --> 00:00:14.180
They are increasingly turning
to governments, health care

00:00:14.180 --> 00:00:17.180
organizations, and other
businesses for information

00:00:17.180 --> 00:00:19.790
using online and phone support.

00:00:19.790 --> 00:00:22.490
This sudden, unprecedented
customer demand

00:00:22.490 --> 00:00:25.580
is overwhelming customer
support resources.

00:00:25.580 --> 00:00:28.610
In this video, we will walk
you through a rapid response

00:00:28.610 --> 00:00:32.000
virtual agent solution, which
is built using a template

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:33.500
that we've open sourced.

00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:36.710
This to help you address
immediate customer inquiries

00:00:36.710 --> 00:00:39.770
and relieve pressure from
your contact centers.

00:00:39.770 --> 00:00:41.500
Let's take a look.

00:00:41.500 --> 00:00:43.200
Here's a web-based example.

00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:46.820
Let's say a user is looking
to know more about COVID-19

00:00:46.820 --> 00:00:48.485
and how it spreads.

00:00:48.485 --> 00:00:50.360
They can just click on
the suggestion bubbles

00:00:50.360 --> 00:00:52.460
like, "What is COVID-19?"

00:00:52.460 --> 00:00:54.410
or "How does it spread?"

00:00:54.410 --> 00:00:57.650
And it responds accordingly
based on WHO and CDC

00:00:57.650 --> 00:00:59.220
recommendations.

00:00:59.220 --> 00:01:01.730
If the user wants to
get a screening done,

00:01:01.730 --> 00:01:04.250
they can just click on
the Start Screening button

00:01:04.250 --> 00:01:06.680
and enter straight
into screening.

00:01:06.680 --> 00:01:09.230
The flow here will depend
on the user selection,

00:01:09.230 --> 00:01:11.870
but let's say none
of those apply.

00:01:11.870 --> 00:01:15.600
They select No and are presented
with some more symptoms.

00:01:15.600 --> 00:01:18.410
Let's say they are experiencing
signs of low blood pressure

00:01:18.410 --> 00:01:21.990
and indicate Yes
in this response.

00:01:21.990 --> 00:01:24.020
The screening indicates
that they should

00:01:24.020 --> 00:01:26.060
seek medical help immediately.

00:01:26.060 --> 00:01:27.800
Let's take an example
of a user whose

00:01:27.800 --> 00:01:30.770
situation is not this serious.

00:01:30.770 --> 00:01:32.600
They start the
screening process,

00:01:32.600 --> 00:01:35.000
don't have any serious
life-threatening symptoms,

00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:39.370
but are experiencing some cough
and minor shortness in breath.

00:01:39.370 --> 00:01:43.430
The screening now gets deeper
into their travel history,

00:01:43.430 --> 00:01:46.160
where they have been
in the last 14 days,

00:01:46.160 --> 00:01:49.790
and then verifies their age
to suggest a course of action,

00:01:49.790 --> 00:01:54.950
or other resources like how
to manage COVID at home.

00:01:54.950 --> 00:01:58.670
If you would like to customize
a solution with your own web UI

00:01:58.670 --> 00:02:02.540
to match with your brand,
you can absolutely do that.

00:02:02.540 --> 00:02:04.050
Here's an example.

00:02:04.050 --> 00:02:07.700
Let's say a user is interested
in knowing the number of cases

00:02:07.700 --> 00:02:09.560
in the United States.

00:02:09.560 --> 00:02:13.250
They can select the auto
suggestion and get a response.

00:02:13.250 --> 00:02:15.410
They can also type
their question.

00:02:15.410 --> 00:02:17.960
Say they are concerned
about receiving packages.

00:02:17.960 --> 00:02:19.940
Is it safe to receive packages?

00:02:19.940 --> 00:02:22.850
The responses are coming
from the same agent.

00:02:22.850 --> 00:02:25.400
It just has a custom UI now.

00:02:25.400 --> 00:02:29.000
If you have users who may want
to call in through the phone

00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:32.250
to ask some questions and
to get screening done,

00:02:32.250 --> 00:02:34.490
you can easily assign
a phone number.

00:02:34.490 --> 00:02:36.710
We have one assigned here.

00:02:36.710 --> 00:02:37.700
Let's call.

00:02:37.700 --> 00:02:38.330
BOT: Hello.

00:02:38.330 --> 00:02:40.880
I am the COVID-19
Rapid Response Bot.

00:02:40.880 --> 00:02:43.580
You can ask me questions
related to COVID-19

00:02:43.580 --> 00:02:46.580
and I will provide some answers
based on publicly available

00:02:46.580 --> 00:02:47.300
information.

00:02:47.300 --> 00:02:50.780
Disclaimer, I do not provide
medical advice, diagnosis,

00:02:50.780 --> 00:02:51.500
or treatment.

00:02:51.500 --> 00:02:54.230
If you are experiencing a
life-threatening emergency,

00:02:54.230 --> 00:02:55.460
call 9-1-1.

00:02:55.460 --> 00:02:56.690
How can I help?

00:02:56.690 --> 00:03:00.460
SPEAKER: What is the difference
between flu and coronavirus?

00:03:00.460 --> 00:03:03.770
BOT: A COVID-19 infection has
the same signs and symptoms

00:03:03.770 --> 00:03:06.290
as the common cold, and you
can only differentiate them

00:03:06.290 --> 00:03:09.410
through laboratory testing
to determine the virus type.

00:03:09.410 --> 00:03:11.090
SPEAKER: Is the virus airborne?

00:03:11.090 --> 00:03:13.370
BOT: Studies to date
suggest that the virus that

00:03:13.370 --> 00:03:16.670
causes COVID-19 is mainly
transmitted through contact

00:03:16.670 --> 00:03:20.060
with respiratory droplets
rather than through the air.

00:03:20.060 --> 00:03:22.100
SPEAKER: As you saw,
the open source template

00:03:22.100 --> 00:03:25.160
is pre-trained with common
COVID-19-related answers

00:03:25.160 --> 00:03:26.690
and triage screener.

00:03:26.690 --> 00:03:30.110
You can enhance and update the
experience as often as needed

00:03:30.110 --> 00:03:31.580
through dialogue flow.

00:03:31.580 --> 00:03:34.040
Please refer to our
documentation for a quick guide

00:03:34.040 --> 00:03:35.240
to get started.

00:03:35.240 --> 00:03:38.590
[MUSIC PLAYING]

